$ nexoctl access rule list mem/media
No access rule on `mem/media`.

$ nexoctl access rule add mem/media --id img-pub --allow --principal * --action read --regex ^img/[0-9]{4}/.*\.(jpe?g|png)$ --ignore-case
Added the access rule `img-pub` to `mem/media` (1 rule).

$ nexoctl access rule add mem/media --id no-private --deny --principal * --action all --glob **/private/** --priority 5
Added the access rule `no-private` to `mem/media` (2 rules).

$ nexoctl access rule add mem/media --id docs --allow --principal user:alice --action read --action list --prefix docs/ --source-ip 10.0.0.0/8 --description documents of alice
Added the access rule `docs` to `mem/media` (3 rules).

$ nexoctl access rule add mem/media --id img-pub --allow --principal * --action read
! nexoctl: error: mem/media: conflict: the access rule "img-pub" exists in `mem/media` (use --replace)
[exit 1]

$ nexoctl access rule add mem/media --id bad --allow --principal * --action read --regex ([
! nexoctl: error: mem/media: invalid argument: invalid access rule: missing closing ]: [ (invalid_access_rule)
[exit 1]

$ nexoctl access rule add mem/media --id x --principal * --action read
! nexoctl: error: one of --allow and --deny is required
! Run 'nexoctl access rule add --help' for usage.
[exit 2]

$ nexoctl access rule add mem/media --id x --allow --principal * --action read --prefix a --glob b
! nexoctl: error: --prefix, --glob and --regex are mutually exclusive
! Run 'nexoctl access rule add --help' for usage.
[exit 2]

$ nexoctl access rule list mem/media
ID                   PRIORITY  EFFECT PRINCIPALS           ACTIONS          MATCH
no-private                  5  deny   *                    all              glob **/private/**
img-pub                   100  allow  *                    read             regex(i) ^img/[0-9]{4}/.*\.(jpe?g|png)$
docs                      100  allow  user:alice           read,list        prefix docs/ (conditions)

$ nexoctl access rule info mem/media --id img-pub
ID: img-pub
Priority: 100
Effect: allow
Principals: *
Actions: read
Match: regex(i) ^img/[0-9]{4}/.*\.(jpe?g|png)$

$ nexoctl access rule info mem/media --id nope
! nexoctl: error: access rule "nope" of `mem/media`: not found
[exit 3]

$ nexoctl access test mem/media/img/2026/a.JPG mem/media/img/2026/private/b.jpg mem/media/docs/x.txt
img/2026/a.JPG: allowed by access rule `img-pub` (anonymous, s3:GetObject)
  rules: allow (matched: img-pub)
img/2026/private/b.jpg: denied by access rule `no-private` (anonymous, s3:GetObject)
  rules: deny (matched: no-private, img-pub)
docs/x.txt: denied (no statement allows it) (anonymous, s3:GetObject)
  rules: none

$ nexoctl access test mem/media/docs/x.txt --principal user:alice --ip 10.1.2.3 -v
docs/x.txt: allowed by access rule `docs` (user:alice, s3:GetObject)
  rules: allow (matched: docs)
  no-private           deny       5  no key
  img-pub              allow    100  no key
  docs                 allow    100  matches
  reason: allowed by access rule docs

$ nexoctl access test mem/media/docs/x.txt --principal user:alice --ip 192.0.2.1
docs/x.txt: denied (no statement allows it) (user:alice, s3:GetObject)
  rules: none

$ nexoctl access rule move mem/media --id img-pub --priority 1
Moved the access rule `img-pub` of `mem/media` to priority 1.

$ nexoctl access rule list mem/media
ID                   PRIORITY  EFFECT PRINCIPALS           ACTIONS          MATCH
no-private                  5  deny   *                    all              glob **/private/**
img-pub                     1  allow  *                    read             regex(i) ^img/[0-9]{4}/.*\.(jpe?g|png)$
docs                      100  allow  user:alice           read,list        prefix docs/ (conditions)

$ nexoctl access export mem/media rules.yaml
Exported 3 access rules of `mem/media` to rules.yaml.

--- rules.yaml
bucket: media
rules:
  - id: img-pub
    priority: 1
    effect: allow
    principals:
      - '*'
    actions:
      - read
    match:
      type: regex
      pattern: ^img/[0-9]{4}/.*\.(jpe?g|png)$
      caseInsensitive: true
  - id: no-private
    priority: 5
    effect: deny
    principals:
      - '*'
    actions:
      - all
    match:
      type: glob
      pattern: '**/private/**'
  - id: docs
    priority: 100
    effect: allow
    principals:
      - user:alice
    actions:
      - read
      - list
    match:
      type: prefix
      pattern: docs/
    conditions:
      sourceIp:
        - 10.0.0.0/8
    description: documents of alice

$ nexoctl access import mem/copy rules.yaml
Imported 3 access rules into `mem/copy`.

$ nexoctl access rule remove mem/media --id docs
Removed the access rule `docs` from `mem/media`.

$ nexoctl access rule remove mem/media --id docs
! nexoctl: error: access rule "docs" of `mem/media`: not found
[exit 3]

$ nexoctl access public get mem/media
`mem/media` is public (custom): img-pub.

$ nexoctl access public set public-read mem/site
Applied the preset `public-read` to `mem/site`: public.

$ nexoctl access public get mem/site
`mem/site` is public (public-read): preset-public-read.

$ nexoctl access block-public status mem
Public access of the cluster `mem`: not blocked (cluster: off, mode reject).

$ nexoctl access block-public on mem/site
Blocked the public access of `mem/site` (mode reject).

$ nexoctl access block-public status mem/site
Public access of `mem/site`: blocked (cluster: off, mode reject, bucket: on).

$ nexoctl access rule add mem/site --id pub2 --allow --principal * --action read
! nexoctl: error: mem/site: access denied: invalid access rule: public access is blocked: a rule cannot allow everyone ("*") (public_access_blocked)
[exit 4]

$ nexoctl access block-public off mem/site
Unblocked the public access of `mem/site`.

$ nexoctl access export mem/media
bucket: media
rules:
  - id: img-pub
    priority: 1
    effect: allow
    principals:
      - '*'
    actions:
      - read
    match:
      type: regex
      pattern: ^img/[0-9]{4}/.*\.(jpe?g|png)$
      caseInsensitive: true
  - id: no-private
    priority: 5
    effect: deny
    principals:
      - '*'
    actions:
      - all
    match:
      type: glob
      pattern: '**/private/**'

